 looked  at it I saw it was a big painting of me  and my coworker in front of the store  depicted like some bodega gods feeding  the poor and sharing love while bright  shining light was coming from us with  the text on the back of the painting  saying I thank God every day that people  like you still exist you are my heroes  Eli after that we didn't see him that  much anymore and heard just one month  later that he was very sick and passed  away so we decided to hang the painting  just behind the counter in the store and  to this day it's still hanging there  rest in paradise Eli comment number six  connection across borders this one time  I was driving on zero Avenue on the  Canadian border parallel to the US  border and there was a small stretch of  road running on both sides it was a  beautiful summer day and I was feeling  amazing a car appeared on the US side  impulsively I waved and smiled out of my  window on the Canadian side and the two  guys on the opposite road  enthusiastically waved back we soon  disappeared from each other sight but I  won't ever forget that moment of  connection across country borders  comment number 7 a love story I work in  a restaurant and a while ago this older  couple would come in every Saturday for  lunch the man would pull out her chair  and open doors for her like a true  gentleman while she patiently waited he  had a walking frame so he struggled but  insisted they would order spaghetti and  share it lady into [ __ ] style gazing  into each other's eyes you could tell  they really loved each other then they  would order cheesecake and share that  too one day he turned up alone ordered  the same but only ate half the spaghetti  and one of the cheesecake takeaway as I  handed him his cheesecake I asked about  his wife he looked at me with tears in  his eyes and told me she's in a better  place now it really showed me to  appreciate the people I have while I  still have them comment number 8 we're  all human when I worked in a busy  supermarket I often had days where  customers would look down on me for  being behind the checkout as if it  wasn't a worthy enough job for them to  engage in conversation with me I  remember one day I had a nasty customer  after nasty customer and this one guy  waiting in line had heard how others  were talking to me or just ignoring me  he apologized to me on their behalf he  spoke to me like a normal person and  made every effort to make sure we were  both engaged in the conversation  he then told me that he placed his  groceries up extra slow because he don't  want to leave until he saw me smiling  and that way he could leave knowing that  I wasn't feeling so bad as he walked off  I noticed two giant tattoos on his calf  muscles there were the patch signs of a  well known gang that day forever changed  my negative stereotypical perceptions  and assumptions of all gang members they  are humans too  just like that guy made me feel human  again comment number nine I think she  was a mermaid I used to have bright teal  and blue hair and would make my eyebrows  the same color with makeup and one day  when I was walking around in a store a  little girl just stopped dead in her  tracks staring at me and went oh my gosh  I love your hair you're so pretty I said  thank you and kept shopping and when I  turned the corner I heard her say mom I  think she was a mermaid I felt so happy  because I mostly heard a lot of Smurf  jokes about my hair and criticism about  my appearance in general for looking  unconventional and it just reminded me  of the beauty of a child's mind in that  moment  comment number 10 are you okay  a woman saved me from killing myself she  pulled up to the sidewalk where I was  sitting and saw being and about to run  into the street when she just asked are  you okay and saved my life  and that's all of them for today I  really hope you guys enjoyed watching  this episode because I want this to be a  regular series on my channel and  obviously that's only possible if you  guys continue to share your answers here  on youtube or on my Instagram and  Twitter like I mentioned in the intro  all the illustrations in this episode  were done by my friend lon  so please show her some kindness help me  thank her for helping me pull off this  episode I'll link her social media in  the description and it'll also be  somewhere on the screen probably right  here really cool story on how this all  happened basically a while ago I spent  almost an entire day just reading  through the comments for the episode  who's one stranger you still remember I  took screenshots of my favorites and  shared them on my Instagram but I was  really annoyed because I also wanted to  share them here on YouTube I just hadn't  thought of a way yet so I thought about  it and I thought it would be cool to  have an illustrated episode of the  comments and at first I tried to  illustrate them myself but then it  turned out very good I'm not very good  at drawing yet hopefully I will be in  the future but so I put on my list of  things to do to find an illustrator and  I think it was just a few days later I  went on Twitter and lawn who was a  stranger to me at the time had also seen  the episode and wanted to tweet an  illustration of her own answer to the  question I saw it I loved it I really  like the way she else rated it so I  messaged her and asked her if she wanted  to illustrate this episode and here we  are it's crazy how things happen my goal  is to hopefully one day be good enough  and have my own style and illustrating  and maybe I could illustrate an entire  episode myself but we'll see that's  pretty much it please  subscribe button if you want to see more  of this and other things on my channel  also make sure to hit the bell next to  it so you'll get notified as soon as I  upload here on YouTube thank you guys  for watching this episode thank you guys  for everything and I'll see you next  week
 

